## Why This Is Asked
Assesses low‑level persistence, streaming resilience, and real‑time UI concerns on iOS. Evaluates MQTT integration, dedup logic, crash recovery, and test strategy under field conditions.

## Key Concepts
- Core Data modeling and migrations
- MQTT streaming on iOS (CocoaMQTT/URLSession)
- In‑memory buffering and deduplication
- Crash‑safe resume and state replay
- Combine and SwiftUI live updates
- Testing streaming edge cases

## Code Example
```javascript
@objc(Device)
class Device: NSManagedObject {
  @NSManaged var id: String
  @NSManaged var name: String?
  @NSManaged var readings: Set<TelemetryReading>
}

@objc(TelemetryReading)
class TelemetryReading: NSManagedObject {
  @NSManaged var id: UUID
  @NSManaged var deviceId: String
  @NSManaged var timestamp: Date
  @NSManaged var temperature: Double
  @NSManaged var battery: Double
  @NSManaged var status: String
  @NSManaged var topic: String
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adjust the dedup strategy for high‑throughput brokers with at‑least‑once delivery?
- How would you measure memory and battery impact under sustained streams?

